# PHASE 7 – ATTENDANCE INTEGRATED INTO CLASS SESSIONS

This is a mandatory architectural rule.

DO NOT create a separate standalone attendance workflow as the primary attendance method.

Attendance must be accessed through:

SCHEDULE → SELECT DATE → SELECT CLASS → OPEN CLASS → STUDENT LIST → MARK ATTENDANCE.

## 7.1 Open Class

When a Sensei or Shihan opens a class:

Display the students eligible for that particular class.

The list should contain:
- Student photograph or initials.
- Student name.
- Belt level.
- Attendance selector.

Each student must have two selectable states:

PRESENT – green.

ABSENT – red.

If ABSENT is selected:
- Reveal an optional absence-reason field.

Provide:
- Mark All Present.
- Mark All Absent.
- Save Attendance.

Show live attendance counts.

Example:

12 Students Enrolled.

9 Present.

3 Absent.

## 7.2 Session-based attendance

Every class occurrence must have its own unique session ID.

Attendance must reference:

- Organisation ID.
- Dojo ID.
- Class schedule ID.
- Session ID.
- Student ID.
- Instructor ID.
- Attendance status.
- Optional absence reason.
- Timestamp.

If three classes happen on one date, attendance must be recorded separately for all three.

Attendance in one session must never automatically mark a student present in another session.

## 7.3 Attendance history

Provide a history view for authorised users.

Show:
- Date.
- Class.
- Student.
- Attendance status.
- Instructor.
- Modification history.

Provide monthly attendance percentages.

Support attendance analytics in Stats.

Sensei should only access assigned class attendance.

